%% OVERVIEW:
%%   PDF/X-1a:2001 was specified in an era when metadata was written into an Info dictionary. 
%% That is all that you need for print-only, since the PDF is not searched by the public.
%% But Info is insufficiently flexible for modern Ebooks and database searches.
%%   Although it is unnecessary and irrelevant, some print services may request XMP metadata,
%% because they are in the habit of also doing Ebooks. Use \pdfx{xmp} to get it.
%% When a print service requests 'without metadata' they mean 'without XMP', which is normal
%% in this context.
%%   With or without XMP, the Info dictionary is written, because it is part of the
%% specification for PDF/X-1a:2001. XMP metadata is XML, so it must conform to the usual
%% XML requirements: some characters are replaced by their Entities.
%%   Your metadata is pre-processed by Lua, called from another page. This page merely
%% inserts that metadata into a template, with some catcode changes for compatibility.


